The time is one o'clock in the afternoon.
Prakash and I go to the cafeteria.
We sit at our usual table.
Prakash eats rice and fish curry.
I eat a sandwich.
We chat happily.
Prakash drinks the office coffee.
Prakash looks into the cup.
Prakash laughs softly.
"Maya, this coffee has no taste," Prakash says.
I laugh.
Then I talk about the badminton game.
"Last Thursday I played badminton," I say.
"I played very well that day."
"That is very good," Prakash says.
We eat our lunch quickly.
The time is now two o'clock.
We walk back to the office.
